# Don't use my definitions to talk about other people's work

Hello I recently learned that some people are getting tired of their work getting framed in terms of my definitions and/or concepts and/or work and/or writing 🥲

So today I am publishing this new blog post / work / concept / definition: 

> Do not use my definitions to talk about other people's work.

If you find yourself in a situation where you are getting tired of someone else framing your work in terms of my definitions, feel free to send them this blog post to make them stop.

It even has a catchy acronym: DUMD TAOP work. (A four four plus four). [NUA](https://www.todepond.com/wikiblogarden/academia/style/never/use/acronyms/).

<br>

More seriously though, rules are made to be broken. Let people be their own person, let them make their own story! For a long time I was personally very tired of constantly getting compared to a small number of other people because it's very reductive and it pins you down to certain ideas. If you're a person who quotes 'me' to frame someone else's work, then you don't understand 'me' at all.

<br>

back to the wikiblogardenite

